I felt I might as well post this, since... I got pretty far, and it'll
be rather short...

Vix the Ranger started off to a rather rocky start, on level one poor
Sirius was killed by a kobold, oh well... I guess this wont end up
being one of those playing pacifist games...

Just for fun I decided... maybe try to play with the "never hit with a
weilded weapon" conduct... and keep going totally vegitarian for
variety. It worked really well... early on was spent tossing Sting at
newts and goblins, as well as crude daggers and a few elven daggers
picked up from hobbits.

In the mines it looked very dangerous though, with a Gnome King and
several Gnome lords all lurking around the entrance, so she decided to
work the other way down... when level four or so came up... there were
two little lonely kitties, one named "Start" and the other named
"DL16" which... looked like a really bad omen, whoever died here must
be like, really high level... or at least kinda well prepared...

A rothe turned up, and was killed rather carefully with a volly of
arrows, Vix was still only around level five or so so it was a little
scary... Digger12's ghost was led out of the way to reveal a yummy
bones pile... nothing really good... While wandering on... two more
ghosts... neither of which looked dangerous... one was on an altar
with mojo, and the other provided a nice Wizard's cloak... this is
pleasent... more wandering and... Vix got stuck in the middle of a
cooredor with a ghost behind her, and a werejackal breathing down her
neck, a few arrows later she got rid of it... behind the werejackal...
another ghost! (Named Zorg this time) with a nyummy wand of
lightning...

Feeling very happy and well prepared Vix went on back to the mines,
worked down to minetown to meet a nice ghost (who had strawberries for
a fruit, yum) and fight off some nasty unicorns with a handy gem, as
well as a rope golem. Feeling happy she took care of a few baby
dragons and a mind flayer in the mines... this game is looking nasty,
and she's surviving great *yays* Further on she encounters a nasty
troll who keeps coming back to life, and is finally taken care of with
the help of a friendly kitten... the bones file there had a magic
lamp, and... a bag of holding which was cursed... so... the quest for
holy water started only to bump into... an air elemental.

Now... air elementals are like, my mid game survival test, Vix
~couldn't handle it at all~ except for using a cursed scroll of
teleport to get out of there...

Much holy water hunting later, she finally headed back to the level
with the air elemental, several wands ready, fire and lightning
identified, and illiterate conduct broken by reading the cursed
scroll, she was ready for some E-word fun ... only one problem. As
soon as vix reached the air elemental level she was immidiately
swallowed by the evil elemental... she was expert in bow by now so the
first effort was to shoot her way out, and maybe have some success...
one volly later... too late... down to 13 hps... that's icky... one
turn left... too many hps to pray, so she read off one of her unided
scrolls of teleport... yay! it worked! she's safe! oh wait... *gets
swallowed by the air elemental again*

dywypi?

*sigh* oh well...
